# Git branch naming — HARD RULE

## Branch name = Jira ticket key ONLY

```
CORRECT: DOC-2405
WRONG:   doc-2405-account-overview-regression
WRONG:   DOC-2405-fix-images
WRONG:   feature/DOC-2405-something
WRONG:   doc-2405
```

The branch name is ALWAYS the Jira ticket key, nothing else.
Format: `DOC-XXXX` — uppercase, hyphen, digits. No prefix, no suffix, no slug, no description.

## Creating a branch — use the helper script

NEVER run `git checkout -b` manually.
ALWAYS use the helper script:

```powershell
cd C:\Gcore_projects\product-documentation
.\.agents\tools\create_branch.ps1 DOC-XXXX
```

The script validates the format, checks out main, pulls, and creates the branch.

## Before every git checkout -b

1. Is the name exactly `DOC-XXXX`?
2. No extra words after the ticket key?

If NO to either — STOP. Use the script.
